{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Noms API","summary":"A REST API for nutritional data: foods, brands, nutrients and food groups.","description":"**Noms** is a REST API for nutritional data: **foods**, **brands**, **nutrients**\nand **food groups**.\n\n## Authentication\n\nSend your API key in the `X-API-Key` header on every `/v1` request:\n\n```\nX-API-Key: noms_sk_...\n```\n\n## Responses\n\n- **Envelope.** Every response is wrapped as `{ \"data\": … }`. List responses also\n  carry `links` (pagination URLs) and `meta` (page info).\n- **Types.** Keys are `snake_case`, timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC (`...Z`), and decimals\n  are JSON **strings** to keep full precision (e.g. `\"12.5000\"`, never a rounded\n  float).\n\n## Querying lists\n\n- **Pagination.** Set a page size with `page_size`, then follow `links.next` until\n  `meta.has_more` is `false`. A cursor stays valid as the catalog changes underneath\n  it, so a page you fetch is never invalidated by one you have not fetched yet. If you\n  sort on a value that can change (a nutrient, a brand name), a row whose value moves\n  while you are paging can repeat or be missed — de-duplicate by `id`, and walk the\n  whole catalog on the default `id` order, which never moves.\n- **Filtering.** `?name[eq]=Milk` (a bare `?name=Milk` defaults to `eq`); operators\n  are `eq`, `in`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte` where the field supports them. Filters\n  match only rows with a present value: on a nullable field, `[eq]=false` (or any\n  comparison) excludes `null` rows. For example, `is_foundational[eq]=false`\n  returns explicitly-`false` foods, not the undetermined (`null`) ones.\n- **Sorting.** `?sort=name` (ascending) or `?sort=-name` (descending); comma-join\n  for tie-breakers.\n- **Text search.** `?q=...` is typo-tolerant — a close-but-misspelled word still\n  finds the right food. With no explicit `sort`, results come back best match\n  first. A `sort` given *alongside* `q` breaks ties within that ordering rather\n  than replacing it — to order strictly by a column, omit `q`.\n- **Sorting by nutrient.** `?sort=-nutrient[PROTEIN]` orders foods by their\n  per-100 g/ml value for a nutrient code. Foods that do not carry the nutrient\n  rank **last** rather than being dropped, so the result count is the same as\n  the unsorted query's.\n- **Sorting by brand.** `?sort=brand_name` orders by the food's brand; unbranded\n  foods rank last, on the same rule.\n- **Sparse fieldsets.** Return only the keys you need with `fields[<resource>]`, e.g.\n  `?fields[foods]=id,name`.\n- **Includes.** `/v1/foods` can embed related resources with `include=`, e.g.\n  `include=brand,food_group,nutrients,serving_sizes,images,market_countries`.\n\n## Errors\n\nEvery error is an **RFC 9457** problem document served as `application/problem+json`,\nwith a stable `type`, a human-readable `title` and `detail`, the HTTP `status`, and\nresource-specific extension members where useful.\n\n## Rate limits\n\nYour account has a request quota for its plan, and every key you hold draws on the same\nallowance — a second key never buys a second quota. The window is a rolling 24 hours on\nthe free plan and your billing period on the paid plans.\nEvery `/v1` resource response carries `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining`, and\n`RateLimit-Reset` headers (plus legacy `X-RateLimit-*` aliases) so you can see where\nyou stand before hitting the wall. Once the quota is exhausted, requests return\n**`429 Too Many Requests`** (an RFC 9457 problem) with a `Retry-After` header. Wait\nuntil the window resets, then retry.\n\n## Free-tier limits\n\nThe free tier is built for **looking things up**, not bulk-downloading the dataset:\n\n- **Search or fetch by id.** List endpoints require a `?q=` search; a bare or\n  filter-only list returns **`403`** (`/problems/enumeration-forbidden`). Any single\n  record is always reachable with `GET /v1/{resource}/{id}`.\n- **Result depth.** Search results are capped at roughly the first **1,000** matches;\n  paging past that returns **`403`** (`/problems/result-depth-exceeded`).\n- **Single market.** The free tier serves **one** market (country). Choose it in the\n  dashboard or with `PUT /v1/market`; until you do, `foods` requests return **`403`**\n  (`/problems/market-not-selected`). After that, `foods` is scoped to that market. The\n  choice belongs to your **account**, so every key you hold shares it.\n\nPaid tiers lift all three: full enumeration, unlimited pagination depth, all markets.\n","contact":{"name":"Noms","url":"https://noms.sh/","email":"support@noms.sh"},"license":{"name":"Proprietary — © Noms, all rights reserved"},"version":"v1","x-logo":{"url":"/wordmark.svg","backgroundColor":"#ffffff","altText":"Noms","href":"https://noms.sh"}},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.noms.sh","description":"Production"}],"paths":{"/v1/foods":{"get":{"tags":["foods"],"summary":"List foods","description":"Return a keyset-paginated page of the food catalog — the primary endpoint.\n\nEmbed related resources with `include=` (`brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`,\n`serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`); filter on columns, relations\n(`brand_name`, `market_countries`), and per-nutrient values\n(`nutrient[CODE][op]`); sort on columns or a nutrient value\n(`sort=-nutrient[PROTEIN]`); trim with `fields[<resource>]`; and search with `?q=`.","operationId":"foodsListFoods","security":[{"ApiKey":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"page_size","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Number of items to return per page (keyset pagination). Allowed range is 1–20; a value outside it is rejected with a 400.","examples":[20],"title":"Page Size"},"description":"Number of items to return per page (keyset pagination). Allowed range is 1–20; a value outside it is rejected with a 400."},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Opaque keyset-pagination cursor. Don't build it by hand; follow `links.next` from a previous response to fetch the next page.","title":"Cursor"},"description":"Opaque keyset-pagination cursor. Don't build it by hand; follow `links.next` from a previous response to fetch the next page."},{"name":"sort","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Sort key; prefix with `-` for descending (`-name`). Comma-join keys for tie-breakers. Defaults to the resource's natural order.","examples":["-name"],"title":"Sort"},"description":"Sort key; prefix with `-` for descending (`-name`). Comma-join keys for tie-breakers. Defaults to the resource's natural order."},{"name":"include","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Comma-separated related resources to embed in each item: `brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`, `serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`. Relations load only when requested.","examples":["brand,nutrients"],"title":"Include"},"description":"Comma-separated related resources to embed in each item: `brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`, `serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`. Relations load only when requested."},{"name":"q","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Typo-tolerant text search. Filters to matching rows and, when no `sort` is given, orders them by relevance. Composes with filters and pagination.","examples":["chocolat"],"title":"Q"},"description":"Typo-tolerant text search. Filters to matching rows and, when no `sort` is given, orders them by relevance. Composes with filters and pagination."},{"name":"fields[foods]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `foods` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[brands]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `brands` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[food-groups]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `food-groups` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[nutrients]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `nutrients` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[serving_sizes]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `serving_sizes` fields to return (e.g. `descriptor,grams`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"descriptor,grams"},{"name":"fields[images]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `images` fields to return (e.g. `type,url`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"type,url"},{"name":"fields[market_countries]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `market_countries` fields to return (e.g. `country_code`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"country_code"},{"name":"barcode","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `barcode`. Bare `barcode=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `barcode[eq]`, `barcode[in]`. `barcode[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"brand_id","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `brand_id`. Bare `brand_id=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `brand_id[eq]`, `brand_id[in]`. `brand_id[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"brand_name","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `brand_name`. Bare `brand_name=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `brand_name[eq]`, `brand_name[in]`. `brand_name[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"country_of_origin","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `country_of_origin`. Bare `country_of_origin=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `country_of_origin[eq]`, `country_of_origin[in]`. `country_of_origin[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"food_group_id","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `food_group_id`. Bare `food_group_id=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `food_group_id[eq]`, `food_group_id[in]`. `food_group_id[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"id","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `id`. Bare `id=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `id[eq]`, `id[in]`. `id[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"is_foundational","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `is_foundational`. Bare `is_foundational=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `is_foundational[eq]`. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"market_countries","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `market_countries`. Bare `market_countries=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `market_countries[eq]`, `market_countries[in]`. `market_countries[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"name","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `name`. Bare `name=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `name[eq]`, `name[in]`. `name[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"nutrient[CODE][op]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on a nutrient's per-100 value. `CODE` is a nutrient id from `GET /v1/nutrients` and `op` is one of `eq`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`. Repeat the parameter to apply several constraints at once. A food with no value recorded for that nutrient never matches.","schema":{"type":"number"},"example":"10"},{"name":"If-None-Match","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"An `ETag` from a previous response for this URL. If it still matches, the API answers `304 Not Modified` with no body; otherwise you get the full `200`. Either way the request is metered.","examples":{"revalidate":{"value":"\"9f2c1b7e4a0d6538bb1c0e2f7a4d9c30\""}}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of foods. Each `data` item is the flat food resource; nested objects (`brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`, `serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`) appear only when requested via `include=`, and `fields[<resource>]` may trim the keys present.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Page_FoodDetailSchema_"}}},"headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"ETag":{"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"A strong entity-tag for this exact response. Send it back as `If-None-Match` on your next request for the same URL: if nothing has changed you get a `304 Not Modified` with no body instead of the full page. The tag covers everything the response depends on — your tier and market, `include`, `fields`, `sort`, and the page cursor — so it is only ever valid for the request that produced it."}}},"422":{"description":"The request was well-formed but could not be processed: a parameter failed validation, or a value is not one this resource accepts.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/validation-error","title":"Request validation error","status":422,"errors":[{"type":"int_parsing","loc":["query","page_size"],"msg":"Input should be a valid integer"}],"detail":"Request validation failed.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/validation-error"}}}},"400":{"description":"Malformed request: an invalid query parameter, cursor, filter, sort, page size, include, or sparse-fieldset selection.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"examples":{"Invalid pagination cursor":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-cursor","title":"Invalid pagination cursor","status":400,"cursor":"bm90LWEtY3Vyc29y","reason":"invalid base64 payload","detail":"Cursor could not be decoded: invalid base64 payload. Follow links.next from a fresh first page rather than constructing a cursor by hand.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-cursor"}},"Invalid filter":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-filter","title":"Invalid filter","status":400,"field":"name","op":"contains","supported_operators":["eq","in"],"supported_fields":["id","name","barcode"],"detail":"Filter 'name' is invalid: operator 'contains' is not supported for 'name'. Supported operators: eq, in.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-filter"}},"Invalid sort":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-sort","title":"Invalid sort","status":400,"column":"created_at","supported_columns":["id","name"],"detail":"Sort column 'created_at' is not sortable on this endpoint. Sortable columns: id, name.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-sort"}},"Invalid page size":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-page-size","title":"Invalid page size","status":400,"requested":0,"minimum":1,"maximum":20,"detail":"page_size=0 is below the minimum of 1","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-page-size"}},"Unknown query parameter":{"value":{"type":"/problems/unknown-query-param","title":"Unknown query parameter","status":400,"param":"page[size]","supported_params":["cursor","page_size","sort"],"suggestion":"page_size","detail":"'page[size]' is not a supported query parameter. Did you mean 'page_size'? Supported parameters: cursor, page_size, sort; plus LHS-bracket filters (e.g. name[eq]).","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/unknown-query-param"}},"Invalid sparse-fieldset selection":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-fields","title":"Invalid sparse-fieldset selection","status":400,"resource":"foods","field":"colour","supported_fields":["id","name","barcode"],"detail":"Field 'colour' is not exposed on resource 'foods'. Exposed fields: id, name, barcode.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-fields"}},"Invalid include":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-include","title":"Invalid include","status":400,"relation":"manufacturer","supported_relations":["brand","food_group","nutrients","serving_sizes","images","market_countries"],"detail":"Relationship 'manufacturer' cannot be included on this endpoint. Supported relationships: brand, food_group, nutrients, serving_sizes, images, market_countries.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-include"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Authentication is missing or invalid.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/unauthorized","title":"Unauthorized","status":401,"detail":"Valid authentication is required to access this resource.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/unauthorized"}}}},"403":{"description":"The request is authenticated but not permitted.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"examples":{"Bulk enumeration not available on this tier":{"value":{"type":"/problems/enumeration-forbidden","title":"Bulk enumeration not available on this tier","status":403,"detail":"This tier does not allow bulk listing. Add a `q` search query to this request, fetch a single item by id, or upgrade for full enumeration.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/enumeration-forbidden"}},"Result depth limit exceeded":{"value":{"type":"/problems/result-depth-exceeded","title":"Result depth limit exceeded","status":403,"cap":1000,"detail":"This tier returns roughly the first 1000 results of a query. Narrow your search with `q` or filters, or upgrade for unlimited pagination depth.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/result-depth-exceeded"}},"No market selected for this tier":{"value":{"type":"/problems/market-not-selected","title":"No market selected for this tier","status":403,"detail":"This tier serves one market and your account has not chosen one yet. Set your market in the dashboard or with `PUT /v1/market`, then retry — or upgrade for all-markets access.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/market-not-selected"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"The key exceeded a rate limit: either its per-window request quota or its short-window burst rate; retry after the `Retry-After` interval (quota responses also carry `RateLimit` headers).","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"examples":{"Rate limit exceeded":{"value":{"type":"/problems/rate-limited","title":"Rate limit exceeded","status":429,"limit":1,"window":"second","retry_after":1,"detail":"Burst rate limit of 1 requests per second exceeded. Slow down and retry after the Retry-After interval.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/rate-limited"}},"Quota exceeded":{"value":{"type":"/problems/quota-exceeded","title":"Quota exceeded","status":429,"limit":250,"window":"daily","retry_after":3600,"detail":"Request quota of 250 per day exceeded. Retry once the current window resets.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/quota-exceeded"}}}}},"headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the quota window resets."}}},"503":{"description":"The service is temporarily unable to handle the request; retry shortly.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"examples":{"Service unavailable":{"value":{"type":"/problems/service-unavailable","title":"Service unavailable","status":503,"detail":"The service is briefly unavailable; retry shortly.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/service-unavailable"}},"Search unavailable":{"value":{"type":"/problems/search-unavailable","title":"Search unavailable","status":503,"detail":"The search service is temporarily unavailable, so this request could not be answered. Retry shortly. Requests that do not use `q` or a nutrient sort are unaffected.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/search-unavailable"}}}}}},"504":{"description":"The `?q=` search outran its time budget and was cancelled; narrow the query and retry.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/search-timeout","title":"Search timed out","status":504,"timeout_ms":800,"detail":"The search exceeded its 800ms time limit and was abandoned. Narrow the query — a more specific `q`, or additional filters — and retry.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/search-timeout"}}}},"500":{"description":"An unexpected server error occurred.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/internal-server-error","title":"Internal server error","status":500,"detail":"An unexpected error occurred while processing the request.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/internal-server-error"}}}},"304":{"description":"Your copy is still current — the `If-None-Match` you sent matches the current entity-tag, so no body is returned. **This still counts against your quota**: the request reached the API, so it is metered and rate-limited exactly like a `200`.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"ETag":{"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"A strong entity-tag for this exact response. Send it back as `If-None-Match` on your next request for the same URL: if nothing has changed you get a `304 Not Modified` with no body instead of the full page. The tag covers everything the response depends on — your tier and market, `include`, `fields`, `sort`, and the page cursor — so it is only ever valid for the request that produced it."}}}}}},"/v1/foods/{id}":{"get":{"tags":["foods"],"summary":"Get a food","description":"Return a single food by its short-id, or a 404 if no food has that id.\n\nEmbed related resources with `include=` and trim with `fields[<resource>]`, the\nsame way the list endpoint does. A **retired** id (one merged into another\nfood) forwards to the surviving food at `200` with an added `canonical_id`\nfield, so a stored id never dead-ends after a merge.","operationId":"foodsGetFood","security":[{"ApiKey":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","description":"Food short-id (12-char base62).","examples":["3f9a1c0b7e2d"],"title":"Id"},"description":"Food short-id (12-char base62)."},{"name":"include","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Comma-separated related resources to embed: `brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`, `serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`.","examples":["brand,nutrients"],"title":"Include"},"description":"Comma-separated related resources to embed: `brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`, `serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`."},{"name":"fields[foods]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `foods` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[brands]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `brands` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[food-groups]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `food-groups` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[nutrients]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `nutrients` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"fields[serving_sizes]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `serving_sizes` fields to return (e.g. `descriptor,grams`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"descriptor,grams"},{"name":"fields[images]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `images` fields to return (e.g. `type,url`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"type,url"},{"name":"fields[market_countries]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `market_countries` fields to return (e.g. `country_code`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"country_code"},{"name":"If-None-Match","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"An `ETag` from a previous response for this URL. If it still matches, the API answers `304 Not Modified` with no body; otherwise you get the full `200`. Either way the request is metered.","examples":{"revalidate":{"value":"\"9f2c1b7e4a0d6538bb1c0e2f7a4d9c30\""}}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A single food. The flat food resource; nested objects (`brand`, `food_group`, `nutrients`, `serving_sizes`, `images`, `market_countries`) appear only when requested via `include=`, and `fields[<resource>]` may trim the keys present. If the requested id was **retired** by a merge, the canonical food is returned with an extra `canonical_id` field naming its live id — update any stored reference to it.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Item_FoodDetailSchema_"}}},"headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"ETag":{"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"A strong entity-tag for this exact response. Send it back as `If-None-Match` on your next request for the same URL: if nothing has changed you get a `304 Not Modified` with no body instead of the full page. The tag covers everything the response depends on — your tier and market, `include`, `fields`, `sort`, and the page cursor — so it is only ever valid for the request that produced it."}}},"422":{"description":"The request was well-formed but could not be processed: a parameter failed validation, or a value is not one this resource accepts.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/validation-error","title":"Request validation error","status":422,"errors":[{"type":"int_parsing","loc":["query","page_size"],"msg":"Input should be a valid integer"}],"detail":"Request validation failed.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/validation-error"}}}},"404":{"description":"No resource matches the requested id.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/not-found","title":"Not found","status":404,"resource":"foods","id":"abc123def456","detail":"Food with id 'abc123def456' was not found.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/not-found"}}}},"400":{"description":"Malformed request: an invalid query parameter, cursor, filter, sort, page size, include, or sparse-fieldset selection.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"examples":{"Unknown query parameter":{"value":{"type":"/problems/unknown-query-param","title":"Unknown query parameter","status":400,"param":"page[size]","supported_params":["cursor","page_size","sort"],"suggestion":"page_size","detail":"'page[size]' is not a supported query parameter. Did you mean 'page_size'? Supported parameters: cursor, page_size, sort; plus LHS-bracket filters (e.g. name[eq]).","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/unknown-query-param"}},"Invalid sparse-fieldset selection":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-fields","title":"Invalid sparse-fieldset selection","status":400,"resource":"foods","field":"colour","supported_fields":["id","name","barcode"],"detail":"Field 'colour' is not exposed on resource 'foods'. Exposed fields: id, name, barcode.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-fields"}},"Invalid include":{"value":{"type":"/problems/invalid-include","title":"Invalid include","status":400,"relation":"manufacturer","supported_relations":["brand","food_group","nutrients","serving_sizes","images","market_countries"],"detail":"Relationship 'manufacturer' cannot be included on this endpoint. Supported relationships: brand, food_group, nutrients, serving_sizes, images, market_countries.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/invalid-include"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Authentication is missing or invalid.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/unauthorized","title":"Unauthorized","status":401,"detail":"Valid authentication is required to access this resource.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/unauthorized"}}}},"429":{"description":"The key exceeded a rate limit: either its per-window request quota or its short-window burst rate; retry after the `Retry-After` interval (quota responses also carry `RateLimit` headers).","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"examples":{"Rate limit exceeded":{"value":{"type":"/problems/rate-limited","title":"Rate limit exceeded","status":429,"limit":1,"window":"second","retry_after":1,"detail":"Burst rate limit of 1 requests per second exceeded. Slow down and retry after the Retry-After interval.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/rate-limited"}},"Quota exceeded":{"value":{"type":"/problems/quota-exceeded","title":"Quota exceeded","status":429,"limit":250,"window":"daily","retry_after":3600,"detail":"Request quota of 250 per day exceeded. Retry once the current window resets.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/quota-exceeded"}}}}},"headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the quota window resets."}}},"503":{"description":"The service is temporarily unable to handle the request; retry shortly.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/service-unavailable","title":"Service unavailable","status":503,"detail":"The service is briefly unavailable; retry shortly.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/service-unavailable"}}}},"500":{"description":"An unexpected server error occurred.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/internal-server-error","title":"Internal server error","status":500,"detail":"An unexpected error occurred while processing the request.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/internal-server-error"}}}},"403":{"description":"The request is authenticated but not permitted.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/market-not-selected","title":"No market selected for this tier","status":403,"detail":"This tier serves one market and your account has not chosen one yet. Set your market in the dashboard or with `PUT /v1/market`, then retry — or upgrade for all-markets access.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/market-not-selected"}}}},"304":{"description":"Your copy is still current — the `If-None-Match` you sent matches the current entity-tag, so no body is returned. **This still counts against your quota**: the request reached the API, so it is metered and rate-limited exactly like a `200`.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"ETag":{"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"A strong entity-tag for this exact response. Send it back as `If-None-Match` on your next request for the same URL: if nothing has changed you get a `304 Not Modified` with no body instead of the full page. The tag covers everything the response depends on — your tier and market, `include`, `fields`, `sort`, and the page cursor — so it is only ever valid for the request that produced it."}}}}}},"/v1/nutrients":{"get":{"tags":["nutrients"],"summary":"List nutrients","description":"Return a keyset-paginated page of the canonical nutrient catalog.\n\nSupports filtering (`id`, `name`, `unit`), sorting, sparse fieldsets\n(`fields[nutrients]`), and typo-tolerant search (`?q=`).","operationId":"nutrientsListNutrients","security":[{"ApiKey":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"page_size","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Number of items to return per page (keyset pagination). Allowed range is 1–20; a value outside it is rejected with a 400.","examples":[20],"title":"Page Size"},"description":"Number of items to return per page (keyset pagination). Allowed range is 1–20; a value outside it is rejected with a 400."},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Opaque keyset-pagination cursor. Don't build it by hand; follow `links.next` from a previous response to fetch the next page.","title":"Cursor"},"description":"Opaque keyset-pagination cursor. Don't build it by hand; follow `links.next` from a previous response to fetch the next page."},{"name":"sort","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Sort key; prefix with `-` for descending (`-name`). Comma-join keys for tie-breakers. Defaults to the resource's natural order.","examples":["-name"],"title":"Sort"},"description":"Sort key; prefix with `-` for descending (`-name`). Comma-join keys for tie-breakers. Defaults to the resource's natural order."},{"name":"q","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Typo-tolerant text search. Filters to matching rows and, when no `sort` is given, orders them by relevance. Composes with filters and pagination.","examples":["chocolat"],"title":"Q"},"description":"Typo-tolerant text search. Filters to matching rows and, when no `sort` is given, orders them by relevance. Composes with filters and pagination."},{"name":"fields[nutrients]","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Sparse fieldset. A comma-separated subset of `nutrients` fields to return (e.g. `id,name`). Omit to return all fields.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"id,name"},{"name":"id","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `id`. Bare `id=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `id[eq]`, `id[in]`. `id[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"name","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `name`. Bare `name=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `name[eq]`, `name[in]`. `name[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"unit","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Filter on `unit`. Bare `unit=value` means `eq`; the bracket form names the operator — `unit[eq]`, `unit[in]`. `unit[in]` takes a comma-separated list. Rows with no value for the field never match.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"If-None-Match","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"An `ETag` from a previous response for this URL. If it still matches, the API answers `304 Not Modified` with no body; otherwise you get the full `200`. Either way the request is metered.","examples":{"revalidate":{"value":"\"9f2c1b7e4a0d6538bb1c0e2f7a4d9c30\""}}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of nutrients. `fields[nutrients]` may trim the keys present in each `data` item.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Page_NutrientSchema_"}}},"headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Your account's request quota for the current window."},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Requests remaining in the current window (floored at 0)."},"RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds until the current window resets."},"X-RateLimit-Limit":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Limit`."},"X-RateLimit-Remaining":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for `RateLimit-Remaining`."},"X-RateLimit-Reset":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Legacy alias for the reset time, as a Unix epoch timestamp (seconds)."},"ETag":{"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"A strong entity-tag for this exact response. Send it back as `If-None-Match` on your next request for the same URL: if nothing has changed you get a `304 Not Modified` with no body instead of the full page. The tag covers everything the response depends on — your tier and market, `include`, `fields`, `sort`, and the page cursor — so it is only ever valid for the request that produced it."}}},"422":{"description":"The request was well-formed but could not be processed: a parameter failed validation, or a value is not one this resource accepts.","content":{"application/problem+json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Problem"},"example":{"type":"/problems/validation-error","title":"Request validation error","status":422,"errors":[{"type":"int_parsing","loc":["query","page_size"],"msg":"Input should be a valid integer"}],"detail":"Request validation failed.","doc_url":"https://api.noms.sh/docs#tag/validati